%% Billing — the life of a payment made outside the platform (cash, cheque, e-transfer).
%% THE SELLER DECIDES: confirmation works from awaiting, claimed or expired, whether or not the
%% buyer ever claimed. The buyer's claim only flags the payment and tells the seller.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> awaiting: order placed, agreements accepted<br/>seller told, buyer shown how to pay

  awaiting --> claimed: buyer says "I sent it" (optional)<br/>seller told once
  claimed --> claimed: buyer adds a note (limited)

  awaiting --> confirmed: seller marks received (cash, e-transfer)<br/>NO buyer claim needed
  claimed --> confirmed: seller marks received
  expired --> confirmed: seller marks received late<br/>the place is taken again first

  awaiting --> received: seller marks a cheque received
  claimed --> received: seller marks a cheque received
  expired --> received: late cheque
  received --> cleared: cheque clears
  received --> bounced: cheque bounces<br/>what it granted is reversed

  awaiting --> rejected: seller says it did not arrive
  claimed --> rejected: seller says it did not arrive

  awaiting --> expired: the hold runs out
  claimed --> expired: the hold runs out

  awaiting --> cancelled: the order is cancelled
  claimed --> cancelled: the order is cancelled

  confirmed --> [*]: payment succeeds, order paid
  cleared --> [*]: payment succeeds (if it was waiting for clearing), order paid
  bounced --> [*]: refund recorded, or payment failed and order cancelled
  rejected --> [*]: payment failed, order cancelled
  cancelled --> [*]
  expired --> [*]: unless the seller confirms later

  note right of claimed
    A claim made after the seller confirmed is ignored.
    A claim after the hold ran out is recorded without
    changing status, so the seller can still confirm.
  end note
